          "ImageDescription": {
            "value": "A pond of <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Pseudacris_crucifer\" title=\"Pseudacris crucifer\">Spring Peepers</a> and <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Rana_sylvatica\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rana sylvatica\">Wood Frogs</a> -- <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Presqu%27ile_Provincial_Park\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Presqu'ile Provincial Park\">Presqu'ile Provincial Park</a>, Ontario, Canada. Field recording of a few hundred individuals in a pond 50 m \u00d7 30 m near Owen Point. The recording was made about an hour after sunset on 2006 April 16. The peepers produce the high \"peeps\" and the wood frogs emit the low, chattering,tones in the background. For their size, spring peepers are extremely loud; this fact can be fully appreciated by turning the playback up.",
